From 1cd214f2cf3403b9a8ad56463af3ea1c8b158fbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:47:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 104/274] Spec decode: greedy verification from vocabulary
 shards

An all-greedy verification step whose logits nothing else reads (no logprobs,
penalties, logit bias, bad words, thinking budget, grammar, top-k/p, min-p)
needs only the target's argmax per verified row. Each rank reduces its
vocabulary shard to a (max, global index) pair; the pairs are all-gathered and
reduced to the first maximum (torch.argmax of the full row, ties included), and
a small kernel applies rejection_sample's greedy rule. This skips the FP32
logits all-gather (2.1 ms a step at 96 rows on TP4) and the full-vocabulary
passes, with the same committed tokens. VLLM_GREEDY_VERIFICATION=0 keeps the
gathered path.

